NAME='Moon'
COVER_SUB='How your emotions work in each sign.'
T=[
('Impulsive','The Moon in Aries sits in Mars’s house and feels first, thinks later: quick irritability, but also intellectual curiosity, initiative, organising ability and a taste for independent work. Emotions are a spark, a whirlwind more than a tide. Jyotish rates the sign neutral for the Moon. Karmic astrology reads the Moon as the soul’s emotional memory, and here the memory is of fighting alone and needing to be first. The shadow is impatience with other people’s moods. The lesson: slow down long enough to hear what you actually feel.'),
('Exalted','The Moon is exalted in Taurus, and Jyotish agrees, making it one of its strongest places. You have a gift for negotiating, a feeling for property and money, and gains that arrive without too much effort, especially in the first decade. The soul settles into comfort: food, music, nature, a warm home. Karmic reading: a memory of security earned, and the lesson of not mistaking it for possession. Feelings rise slowly and leave slowly. The shadow is stubbornness. The lesson: security is built inside as well as owned outside.'),
('Curious','The Moon in Gemini gives literary gifts, a curiosity wide more than deep and a love of travel. Intuition helps in hard moments, though interest in many things at once can slide into hesitation. Jyotish counts Mercury as a friend of the Moon, so heart and mind get along. Moods change quickly and you are charming and hard to pin down. Karmic reading: a past of words, restlessness and many roles. The shadow is overthinking. The lesson: some emotions need a moment of silence, not an explanation.'),
('Own sign','The Moon is at home in Cancer, an ideal placement, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength. It brings a good memory that serves learning, a rich imagination and a love of poetry, music, history and archaeology, with emotional balance and attachment to family and tradition. The old image is a rounded boat carrying what must be kept. Karmic reading: a deep past of belonging, and the task of turning inherited feeling into your own shelter. Under stress it is changeable and capricious. The lesson: you can nurture others without carrying everyone’s weight.'),
('Warm and proud','The Moon in Leo is a guest in the Sun’s sign, and Jyotish counts the Sun as the Moon’s friend. It brings personal luck, vitality, a libertarian and idealistic spirit, a lively imagination and a magnetic, generous personality that draws loyal followers. Ambitions are strong. Under strain it turns to bluff and megalomania. Karmic reading: a soul that carries a memory of recognition and now needs to feel lovable without applause. The shadow is pride and drama. The lesson: you are lovable even when nobody is watching.'),
('Careful','The Moon in Virgo has a strongly intuitive mind, drawn to the unseen world: presentiments, premonitory dreams and a drive to emerge in work. Jyotish treats Mercury as the Moon’s friend. Emotions are filtered through analysis; you show love through practical help and worry quietly. The old image is the seed and the patient plowman. Karmic reading: a soul purifying old emotional habits through service. The shadow is anxiety and perfectionism. The lesson: you are allowed to rest before everything is done.'),
('Gracious','The Moon in Libra, in Venus’s house and Saturn’s exaltation, favours intelligence and artistic gifts. A lively imagination may turn wordy. The spirit is conciliatory: better a friendly solution than a legal fight. Jyotish rates the sign neutral. You need harmony and company, and you mirror the mood of whoever you are with. Karmic reading: memories of relationships and the lesson of standing as one. The shadow is avoiding conflict. The lesson: your own feelings count even when they disturb the peace.'),
('Fall','The Moon is in fall in Scorpio, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here: one of the most problematic placements. Sensitivity is intense and can show as mediumistic gifts, a den where desire and memory are kept. Under strain it turns tyrannical and possessive, with a restless search for pleasure and escape from reality. You love deeply, hold grudges and read hidden motives. Karmic reading: old wounds of trust, betrayal and control, resurfacing to be healed. The lesson: vulnerability is not defeat, and letting go is part of the power you seek.'),
('Free-spirited','The Moon in Jupiter’s house gives vitality, sensitivity, attachment to family and tradition, a taste for physical exercise and a pull toward distant countries. Intuition is happy, with a gift for divination and sensing. Jyotish rates the sign neutral. You need space, humour and a horizon. Under strain: confusion, apathy and melancholy. Karmic reading: memories of journeys and of faith, and the task of staying present. The shadow is restlessness and running from heavy feelings. The lesson: staying through a difficult moment can be its own adventure.'),
('Detriment','The Moon is in detriment in Capricorn, in Saturn’s house: it stays defrauded of its potential, the heart guarded and feelings ruled by discipline. With harmony it promotes social advancement, protection by influential people and success by personal merit, with great analytical ability. Jyotish rates the sign neutral. Karmic reading: a soul that took adult duty early and carries its fears. Under strain: hesitation, slowness and caprice. The shadow is coldness and pessimism. The lesson: needing comfort is not weakness.'),
('Detached','The Moon in Aquarius, domicile of Uranus in the modern view and of Saturn in the classical one, brings original ideas, intellectual curiosity and scientific intuition. Friendships, especially with women, help reach goals. Emotions are watched from a distance: calm in a crisis, hard to reach. Jyotish treats the sign as neutral. The old image is a birth, a tear through which the new is carried. Karmic reading: a soul learning to belong without dissolving. The shadow is too much head, too little heart. The lesson: closeness does not threaten your independence.'),
('Dreamy','The Moon in Pisces favours sensitivity, intuition and mediumship, a rich imagination and a love of music, poetry and painting. Hesitation and suggestibility can weaken initiative. Jyotish treats the sign as neutral for the Moon. The old image is something soft and dissolving, and you absorb moods, atmospheres and other people’s pain. Karmic reading: an old, tired memory that asks for release. The shadow is escapism and taking on other people’s problems. The lesson: compassion also means looking after yourself.'),
]
